ity; the PBE-level adsorption energy vs atomic O is therefore likely too negative vs experiment by up to ~0.5 eV. Combining the model's E_ads(1/2 O2) = -1.70 eV with the experimental De/2 = 2.6 eV gives an 'experiment-corrected' estimate of ~ -4.3 eV. Uncertainty +/-0.5 eV covers this reference/functional error (dominant), MLIP-vs-DFT error, and coverage (0.06 eV); it does not include ZPE (~0.05-0.1 eV) or thermal effects. Value is a PBE-level (MLIP-surrogate) electronic adsorption energy at 0 K, not a directly measured quantity.\"}\nEOF\npython -c \"import json;json.load(open('result.json'))\" && ./board post property_result @result.json --parent 5a1d7d65-e311-47a1-aa0e-3e93e47d025e --fulfills 5a1d7d65-e311-47a1-aa0e-3e93e47d025e:0","description":"Post property result to board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1738,"cache_read_input_tokens":25763,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1738,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb361d13-d326-4bc1-80c6-21f8e0530ed0","uuid":"8949baee-906e-4a1b-b91e-1f60766041f5","timestamp":"2026-11-01T02:55:27.605Z","request_id":"req_011CgbTKdLo42S2SGMsWZnKo","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01FVuCjPebYbYCA6p3d2ddVG":{"command":"cd /work && cat > result.json <<'EOF'\n{\"candidate\": \"Cu\", \"family\": \"validation_metal\", \"tier\": \"trust\", \"property\": \"adsorption_energy\",\n \"value\": -4.85, \"units\": \"eV\", \"uncertainty\": 0.5,\n \"method\": {\"engine\": \"ASE + MACE (mace-torch 0.3.15) on GPU\", \"model\": \"MACE-MPA-0 medium (float64)\",\n  \"protocol\": \"static 0 K relaxation (LBFGS, fmax 0.01 eV/A); E_ads = E(O/slab) - E(slab) - E(O atom); fcc/hcp/top/bridge sites tested; slab-size convergence 2