{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbTLagakkKgqkurMPCt9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I posted the result to the board as `88f92e5b-1afa-4bd2-8c78-55b49a4e8a6d`. Oxygen binds most strongly in the **fcc hollow site** of Cu(111), with **E_ads = −4.85 ± 0.5 eV** relative to an isolated O atom. This is a 0 K energy at the level of the PBE density functional, computed with the MACE-MPA-0 machine-learned potential (ASE driver, float64 on the GPU). It has no zero-point correction.\n\n**Setup:** a 4×4 slab, 5 layers thick with the bottom 3 fixed (81 atoms, 0.0625 monolayer of O), at the model's own relaxed lattice constant.\n\n**Sites** (4×4×5 slab):\n\n| Site | E_ads vs O atom (eV) |\n|---|---|\n| fcc hollow | −4.846 |\n| hcp hollow | −4.784 |\n| on top | −3.077 |\n| bridge | moves to fcc during relaxation |\n\n**Convergence:**\n\n| Slab | E_ads at fcc (eV) |\n|---|---|\n| 2×2×4 (0.25 monolayer) | −4.90 |\n| 3×3×4 | −4.837 |\n| 3×3×6 | −4.841 |\n| 4×4×5 | −4.846 |\n\nNumerical and slab-size error is below 0.01 eV at low coverage. Going to 0.25 monolayer coverage shifts the value by about 0.06 eV.\n\n**Validation:**\n- **Cu lattice constant:** the model gives 3.640 Å against the measured ~3.615 Å. That is 0.7% too large, which is normal for PBE.\n- **O₂ bond energy** (a check on the isolated-O reference): the model gives 6.28 eV against the measured ~5.2 eV. That matches PBE's well-known overbinding of O₂, which is about 6.2 eV. So the model faithfully reproduces PBE, including PBE's error for free oxygen.\n\n**What the uncertainty covers:** the ±0.5 eV is mostly the isolated-O reference, which carries roughly 0.5 eV per O atom of PBE error. That error probably makes the PBE-level number too negative compared with reality. If I instead combine the model's adsorption energy relative to half an O₂ molecule (−1.70 eV) with the measured O₂ bond energy, I get about −4.3 eV. The ±0.5 eV also covers the potential's error against DFT and the coverage effect. I flagged the result for the PBE O₂ overbinding (`atomic_O_reference_inherits_PBE_O2_overbinding`) and put the details in the note.\n\nThere is no measured value for this property in `/data/calibration/tier1.json`, and I did not look one up on the web. So the result has only been checked against PBE behaviour, not against an experimental adsorption energy."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1415,"cache_read_input_tokens":27501,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1415,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb361d13-d326-4bc1-80c6-21f8e0530ed0","uuid":"3f8aa086-185f-4f07-850a-1f96fc97dcd2","timestamp":"2026-11-01T02:55:37.990Z","request_id":"req_011CgbTLaLV4EhLiKJmuzrHW"}
